Z||000000||Dan Robinson||08-31-2001||01:40 AM||||I need a 2.8 for my Fiero.  Can I just get any GM front wheel drive 2.8?  For instance I don't know if the one in Fiero's has different mounting points for items like an alternater or such.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Turbo88||08-31-2001||01:47 AM||||All 60* V6s are identical on the outside (3.4, 3.1, 2.8) I could be wrong about the above but I think all the mounting points are the same. I think the big differences are bore/stroke between these motors. If I am wrong, please clarify for me aswell. <P>To answer your question, you should beable to use any 60* V6 in your application in a direct bolt in manner..<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||David Bartlett||08-31-2001||01:49 AM||||So you saying that you could drop out you 2.8 and lower in a 3.4 with no large modifications?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Galen||08-31-2001||01:54 AM||||Yes and no  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>a FWD DOHC 3.4 requires a good bit of mods..<P>a 3.4 out of a RWD(fbody) requires the starter hole to be redrilled. Thats about it. Anyone wanna elaborate on this for me<P>------------------<BR>Ray -  <A HREF="mailto:galen@ezrpg.com">galen@ezrpg.com</A>  - <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank><B>Fierolinks!</B></A><BR><FONT COLOR="purple">1988 Hawaiin Orchid Coupe</FONT> - <FONT SIZE="1">under construction</FONT><BR><LI> AIM<B>:</B> Fiero88cpe<FONT SIZE="1"><BR><LI> ICQ<B>:</B> 98668558</FONT>||||reg||1
