Z||000006||isthiswhereiputausername?||08-31-2001||06:43 AM||||I have a 2.8 bolted in mine out of a 85 skylark currently.. <P>Wasnt too much work.. (switched from the duke)<P>thinking of a caddy motor this fall  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||JetroGT||08-31-2001||04:41 PM||||Did you have to relocate the starter?||||reg||1
Z||000008||isthiswhereiputausername?||08-31-2001||04:50 PM||||Didnt have to relocate the starter or anything..  I had to build an alt. bracket and modify my exhaust due to the headers coming out at the back.. (this was a quick job I did on my day off with my daily driver, so I didnt bother trying to change manifolds)<P>It fit in great and have no problems with it at all..  <BR>wiring was simple (carbed) <P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Jim Jimenez||09-01-2001||12:37 AM||||Dan:<BR>welcome to the forum. If you are looking for an identical engine assembly,1985 and 1986 celebrities and Cavaliers with a 2.8 W are a dead ringer. 3.1T engines from a U van, too.<BR> Since you are in Milwaukee, just call up Engine and Trans Exchg and they will build you one, and warranty the thing for 3years/75,000 miles||||reg||1
